WEBVTT

1
00:02:07.683 --> 00:02:09.497
<i>Father...</i>

2
00:02:11.583 --> 00:02:13.863
<i>where are you?</i>

3
00:05:35.616 --> 00:05:37.483
<i>Father...</i>

4
00:05:37.782 --> 00:05:40.063
<i>speak to me.</i>

5
00:09:56.549 --> 00:09:58.616
I have water for you here, Yeshua.

6
00:10:00.249 --> 00:10:03.096
That's what your mother calls you, isn't it?

7
00:10:05.216 --> 00:10:08.197
Any name that's good enough for Mary
is good enough for me.

8
00:10:14.949 --> 00:10:17.596
And what does your father call you?

9
00:10:53.249 --> 00:10:55.096
Yeshua.

10
00:12:03.215 --> 00:12:05.029
Hello?

11
00:12:45.399 --> 00:12:48.512
I'm looking for water. I can work for it.

12
00:12:50.882 --> 00:12:52.516
- What can you do?
- Whatever's needed.

13
00:12:52.616 --> 00:12:56.328
You're building up here.
I know carpentry and stone.

14
00:13:05.815 --> 00:13:10.129
- Where are you headed?
- Jerusalem, but I'm a little lost.

15
00:13:17.049 --> 00:13:19.250
Where are you coming from?

16
00:13:19.349 --> 00:13:21.749
From spending time in the desert.

17
00:13:21.849 --> 00:13:24.645
Why? There's nothing here.

18
00:13:29.615 --> 00:13:31.945
What is Jerusalem like?

19
00:13:34.281 --> 00:13:36.870
Dirty and corrupt.

20
00:13:37.715 --> 00:13:41.412
But also alive. Very alive.

21
00:13:43.248 --> 00:13:46.716
- Do you have a father?
- Yes. He's out.

22
00:13:46.816 --> 00:13:50.316
- He'll ask me if I offered you food.
- That's not necessary.

23
00:13:51.415 --> 00:13:53.365
Thank you.

24
00:13:53.465 --> 00:13:57.196
Stay. Please. Rest for a while.

25
00:14:16.215 --> 00:14:19.974
Talking to your father
is like talking to a rock.

26
00:14:21.248 --> 00:14:25.717
He's so busy with his little things,
the shape of a drop of dew,

27
00:14:25.817 --> 00:14:29.817
the sound roots make breaking
their way through the ground.

28
00:14:29.917 --> 00:14:32.882
Everything matters more to him than you.

29
00:14:32.982 --> 00:14:34.882
No.

30
00:14:34.982 --> 00:14:37.345
My father loves me.

31
00:14:39.149 --> 00:14:41.815
He is amused by you.

32
00:14:41.915 --> 00:14:44.378
He loves himself only.

33
00:14:49.248 --> 00:14:51.248
Are you lost?

34
00:14:51.348 --> 00:14:52.612
No.

35
00:14:54.315 --> 00:14:56.817
Are you one of those preachers?

36
00:14:56.917 --> 00:15:01.559
Looking for something here in the desert
that you can't find anywhere else?

37
00:15:04.349 --> 00:15:08.070
How long have you been out here, holy man?

38
00:15:08.782 --> 00:15:11.850
Since the last full moon.
Maybe a little longer.

39
00:15:11.950 --> 00:15:13.383
Alone?

40
00:15:13.483 --> 00:15:17.145
No. You people are never alone.

41
00:15:17.716 --> 00:15:21.935
Some spirit or something
is always with you, isn't it?

42
00:15:23.715 --> 00:15:28.249
Tell me one thing you've learned out here,
and I'll offer you shelter for the night.

43
00:15:28.349 --> 00:15:32.746
- Oh, that's not necessary.
- Please. It would give me pleasure.

44
00:15:35.281 --> 00:15:38.181
Man makes do anywhere.

45
00:15:38.481 --> 00:15:41.022
Because he is man.

46
00:15:42.115 --> 00:15:43.979
Good.

47
00:15:44.632 --> 00:15:46.537
Give me a hand with this.

48
00:15:59.082 --> 00:16:00.945
Thank you.

49
00:16:45.982 --> 00:16:50.931
- There's no need to wait for her.
- I don't mean to offend, but I'm fasting.

50
00:16:57.615 --> 00:16:59.884
What is it?

51
00:16:59.984 --> 00:17:04.080
She thinks it's funny
that she wants to eat but can't...

52
00:17:04.180 --> 00:17:07.540
and our guest, who can, won't.

53
00:17:49.248 --> 00:17:51.711
What are you building up there?

54
00:17:52.081 --> 00:17:55.044
A house for me to live in.

55
00:17:55.816 --> 00:18:00.483
My father wants me to stay here.
To help him make something of this place.

56
00:18:00.883 --> 00:18:03.278
Is that what you want?

57
00:18:05.849 --> 00:18:08.445
What is it that you want?

58
00:18:13.215 --> 00:18:15.879
I want to go to Jerusalem.

59
00:18:16.181 --> 00:18:18.250
And I want to see the sea.

60
00:18:18.350 --> 00:18:21.416
And I want to see
the lighthouse at Alexandria.

61
00:18:21.516 --> 00:18:24.211
And does your father know that?

62
00:18:25.081 --> 00:18:26.716
No.

63
00:18:26.816 --> 00:18:29.678
Why don't you talk to him about it?

64
00:18:38.248 --> 00:18:40.046
I've seen Jerusalem.

65
00:18:40.146 --> 00:18:43.478
<i>I've walked away without my father
knowing and I've seen it from a ridge.</i>

66
00:18:45.148 --> 00:18:49.197
<i>It shines in the sun and I want it
so much, I could scream.</i>

67
00:18:54.948 --> 00:18:57.649
I don't want to waste my time here.

68
00:18:57.749 --> 00:19:00.211
Wasting life is a sin.

69
00:19:01.215 --> 00:19:04.144
I want to leave my footprint on the world.

70
00:19:08.365 --> 00:19:10.895
Come, holy man.

71
00:19:15.582 --> 00:19:17.915
Oh, this isn't necessary.
I can sleep outside.

72
00:19:18.015 --> 00:19:20.611
No. She won't bother you.

73
00:20:16.215 --> 00:20:18.111
Rabbi?

74
00:20:19.248 --> 00:20:21.078
Rabbi.

75
00:20:24.715 --> 00:20:28.144
I've committed a horrible sin.

76
00:20:29.415 --> 00:20:33.068
My son is not my husband's son.

77
00:20:33.682 --> 00:20:36.411
I don't want to die...

78
00:20:36.915 --> 00:20:40.244
and leave this lie behind me.

79
00:20:43.649 --> 00:20:47.502
I don't want my son trapped here forever.

80
00:20:49.081 --> 00:20:52.020
Help me, please.

81
00:23:08.915 --> 00:23:12.483
In your holy man comings-and-goings...

82
00:23:12.583 --> 00:23:15.345
have you learned any medicine?

83
00:23:19.215 --> 00:23:22.081
Cures are the only things worth seeking.

84
00:23:22.181 --> 00:23:26.212
For pain... suffering.

85
00:23:27.015 --> 00:23:30.345
The rest is just...

86
00:23:33.248 --> 00:23:36.548
This boy is good at taking care of the sick.

87
00:23:36.981 --> 00:23:40.044
He's had practice, unfortunately.

88
00:23:40.881 --> 00:23:45.677
If he had come into this world somewhere
else, he could have made it his life's work.

89
00:23:46.715 --> 00:23:49.777
And what did you want for yourself
when you were a boy?

90
00:23:50.482 --> 00:23:53.483
I wanted to raise livestock...

91
00:23:53.682 --> 00:23:57.128
and be a butcher, like my father.

92
00:23:57.648 --> 00:24:00.518
He never taught me any of it, though.

93
00:24:00.681 --> 00:24:05.915
He said it had taken him years and years

94
00:24:06.015 --> 00:24:10.844
to master the skill on his own,
and he wasn't just going to give it away.

95
00:24:12.148 --> 00:24:16.415
"Every man must make himself."
I heard that a thousand times.

96
00:24:16.515 --> 00:24:18.944
He was a selfish man.

97
00:24:20.548 --> 00:24:23.044
And he died alone.

98
00:24:24.781 --> 00:24:26.916
What does your father do?

99
00:24:27.016 --> 00:24:29.949
Ask for permission
when you address a guest, boy.

100
00:24:30.049 --> 00:24:33.311
That's all right. We spoke some yesterday.

101
00:24:34.515 --> 00:24:36.948
My father's a carpenter.

102
00:24:37.448 --> 00:24:39.250
Smart man.

103
00:24:39.649 --> 00:24:43.710
A man who is good at work like that
can always provide for his children.

104
00:24:46.516 --> 00:24:50.786
And did you want to be a carpenter also
when you were a boy?

105
00:25:06.015 --> 00:25:09.322
Your good intentions will be wasted here.

106
00:25:10.016 --> 00:25:14.278
They don't need us to ruin their lives.
They'll do that all by themselves.

107
00:25:14.915 --> 00:25:17.230
Do you know what I do
when they're finally mine?

108
00:25:17.330 --> 00:25:22.244
I have them watch the life they've lived
over and over again. Forever.

109
00:25:23.381 --> 00:25:25.848
Oh, what anger.

110
00:25:25.948 --> 00:25:28.511
You are your father's son.

111
00:25:30.148 --> 00:25:33.114
Very well. I'll stay out of it. Surprise me.

112
00:25:33.214 --> 00:25:36.878
- And if I do?
- A wager?

113
00:25:39.115 --> 00:25:42.066
If you can solve
this entanglement, this knot...

114
00:25:42.166 --> 00:25:46.427
to the satisfaction of the mother,
the father and the child,

115
00:25:46.526 --> 00:25:49.988
I'll stay out of your way
for the rest of your journey home.

116
00:25:54.914 --> 00:25:57.082
And if I fail?

117
00:25:57.182 --> 00:25:59.844
Failure is its own punishment.

118
00:26:01.215 --> 00:26:05.245
- That's Daddy talk.
- Enough for the day.

119
00:26:10.848 --> 00:26:14.316
This is all just an excuse
to delay your departure, isn't it?

120
00:26:14.416 --> 00:26:17.781
Because you're scared to go on.
Scared out of your head.

121
00:26:17.881 --> 00:26:20.332
You're not ready and you know it.

122
00:27:50.447 --> 00:27:52.278
Here.

123
00:28:49.514 --> 00:28:52.011
What part of a bird doesn't fly?

124
00:28:52.981 --> 00:28:56.498
It's a riddle.
What part of a bird doesn't fly?

125
00:28:58.981 --> 00:29:00.914
I don't know.

126
00:29:01.014 --> 00:29:03.044
Its shadow.

127
00:29:04.514 --> 00:29:06.749
- Did you make that up?
- Yes.

128
00:29:06.849 --> 00:29:08.978
It's good.

129
00:29:13.330 --> 00:29:14.928
Yes.

130
00:29:26.848 --> 00:29:29.878
I want the boy to learn a trade.

131
00:29:32.048 --> 00:29:34.944
There's plenty for him to learn right here.

132
00:29:37.081 --> 00:29:39.948
Any trade that he wants.

133
00:29:40.347 --> 00:29:43.078
Or that you want for him.

134
00:29:43.781 --> 00:29:46.844
In Jerusalem, perhaps.

135
00:29:52.981 --> 00:29:55.049
I want this very much.

136
00:29:55.149 --> 00:29:59.449
I would need money for that.
Just to get him set up and started.

137
00:29:59.549 --> 00:30:03.347
No one will take him
as an apprentice without payment.

138
00:30:03.447 --> 00:30:06.477
For food, at least.

139
00:30:07.580 --> 00:30:09.381
Impossible.

140
00:30:10.480 --> 00:30:12.681
You are...

141
00:30:13.580 --> 00:30:16.015
a powerful...

142
00:30:16.414 --> 00:30:18.181
resourceful...

143
00:30:18.280 --> 00:30:20.915
beautiful man...

144
00:30:21.015 --> 00:30:23.744
and you will find a way.

145
00:30:24.814 --> 00:30:27.178
I know it.

146
00:30:36.148 --> 00:30:39.427
I cannot do my dying while he's here.

147
00:30:49.431 --> 00:30:53.461
My father was 47 when he had me.
My mother was 20.

148
00:30:54.714 --> 00:30:58.315
He had another wife before her, but she died.

149
00:30:58.815 --> 00:31:01.624
And now my mother will die too.

150
00:31:02.714 --> 00:31:05.179
And my father says a man makes his own luck.

151
00:31:06.247 --> 00:31:08.111
No.

152
00:31:09.180 --> 00:31:12.048
What did he do to make two wives die?

153
00:31:12.847 --> 00:31:14.648
Nothing.

154
00:31:15.048 --> 00:31:17.277
I agree with you.

155
00:31:24.881 --> 00:31:27.944
Do you have a wife or children?

156
00:31:30.848 --> 00:31:33.177
Do you plan to?

157
00:31:35.581 --> 00:31:38.111
Well, you never know, right?

158
00:31:47.348 --> 00:31:50.515
- Have you ever sailed on a boat?
- Yes, I have.

159
00:31:50.615 --> 00:31:54.380
- Is it scary?
- It can be terrifying.

160
00:31:54.480 --> 00:31:56.961
But mostly it's thrilling.

161
00:32:05.814 --> 00:32:08.544
My father sailed on a boat once.

162
00:32:11.314 --> 00:32:14.277
He said he got caught in a storm at sea.

163
00:32:14.648 --> 00:32:17.111
He said it was a nightmare.

164
00:32:19.114 --> 00:32:22.778
Everything outside of our world
is scary to him.

165
00:35:38.748 --> 00:35:42.510
My father says once my mother
is buried here that we cannot leave.

166
00:35:45.314 --> 00:35:48.610
He says a grave ties a man
to the land forever.

167
00:35:52.481 --> 00:35:55.639
Do you think I'm selfish
because I don't want to live here?

168
00:35:55.739 --> 00:35:57.219
No.

169
00:35:57.749 --> 00:36:00.610
My father has lived here his whole life...

170
00:36:01.047 --> 00:36:03.844
and he's lived it the way he wanted to.

171
00:36:04.914 --> 00:36:07.844
But now it's my turn. Men take turns.

172
00:36:12.347 --> 00:36:14.748
I am not a bad son.

173
00:36:15.147 --> 00:36:17.177
I'm not.

174
00:36:27.581 --> 00:36:30.410
I am not a bad son!

175
00:36:32.380 --> 00:36:35.943
I am not a bad son!

176
00:36:37.310 --> 00:36:39.976
I'm not a bad son!

177
00:36:48.047 --> 00:36:51.377
I am not a bad son!

178
00:39:00.214 --> 00:39:01.645
<i>Rabbi?</i>

179
00:39:03.813 --> 00:39:05.709
Rabbi!

180
00:39:06.880 --> 00:39:09.177
It hurts.

181
00:39:11.080 --> 00:39:13.780
I want it to be over.

182
00:39:14.080 --> 00:39:16.611
I'm not afraid of death.

183
00:39:17.248 --> 00:39:22.110
I'm only scared of being alone
when I get there.

184
00:39:23.347 --> 00:39:25.877
You will not be alone.

185
00:39:27.580 --> 00:39:30.012
None of us is alone.

186
00:39:38.280 --> 00:39:42.091
Find better words, Yeshua.
You must work at that.

187
00:39:42.480 --> 00:39:44.847
Intention is good, but...

188
00:39:44.947 --> 00:39:48.010
often the words are hollow and useless.

189
00:39:48.680 --> 00:39:50.947
Or better still...

190
00:39:51.047 --> 00:39:53.280
find an action.

191
00:39:53.380 --> 00:39:55.244
Yes.

192
00:39:55.913 --> 00:39:58.610
Action over words. Always.

193
00:40:00.080 --> 00:40:02.477
Otherwise, silence.

194
00:41:55.214 --> 00:41:58.010
You think you are his only child?

195
00:42:00.579 --> 00:42:02.910
There are others.

196
00:42:05.247 --> 00:42:07.143
No.

197
00:42:07.847 --> 00:42:10.244
There is only me.

198
00:42:12.414 --> 00:42:14.910
There is only me.

199
00:42:34.813 --> 00:42:37.344
Look in on your mother.

200
00:42:52.381 --> 00:42:56.047
Did the boy speak with you
when you went to the water?

201
00:42:56.147 --> 00:42:58.210
A little.

202
00:43:03.147 --> 00:43:07.049
I don't know how to talk to him.
The words get caught in my throat.

203
00:43:07.149 --> 00:43:12.214
I fight to push them through
and they come out harsh.

204
00:43:12.314 --> 00:43:14.971
I suppose he thinks I'm angry at him.

205
00:43:17.113 --> 00:43:19.476
He doesn't know me...

206
00:43:20.347 --> 00:43:22.877
and I don't know him.

207
00:43:30.147 --> 00:43:33.464
Any words of advice, holy man?

208
00:43:35.314 --> 00:43:38.526
Talk to him about something
that he's interested in.

209
00:43:39.847 --> 00:43:42.310
What is he interested in?

210
00:43:45.113 --> 00:43:46.815
Riddles.

211
00:43:46.915 --> 00:43:49.797
He makes up a very good riddle.

212
00:43:52.880 --> 00:43:55.074
I don't like riddles.

213
00:44:11.713 --> 00:44:15.381
That shooting star last night.
You enjoyed that.

214
00:44:15.480 --> 00:44:18.081
- It was a bore.
- Liar.

215
00:44:18.181 --> 00:44:21.209
I am a liar. That is the truth.

216
00:44:24.947 --> 00:44:28.247
I've seen every shooting star
since the first one.

217
00:44:28.347 --> 00:44:30.977
Every flash of lightning.

218
00:44:31.247 --> 00:44:34.947
I've heard the last gasp
of each thing that ever lived.

219
00:44:35.047 --> 00:44:37.348
Nothing's interesting anymore.

220
00:44:37.447 --> 00:44:41.110
Nothing surprises you? Not a thing?

221
00:44:46.080 --> 00:44:48.513
The repetitiveness.

222
00:44:48.613 --> 00:44:53.782
The obstinate, dull repetitiveness of your
father's plan is bewildering to me.

223
00:44:54.082 --> 00:44:58.813
The same lives lived over
and over and over and over again.

224
00:44:58.913 --> 00:45:01.048
Is there a plan?

225
00:45:01.148 --> 00:45:05.436
It all has to turn into something, it has to
pour out into something, but into what?

226
00:45:06.147 --> 00:45:08.843
And that's my weakness...

227
00:45:09.713 --> 00:45:12.077
curiosity.

228
00:45:14.114 --> 00:45:17.379
But I'll stay as long as it takes, forever...

229
00:45:17.479 --> 00:45:19.513
to witness the end.

230
00:45:19.613 --> 00:45:22.359
The final sunset. If there is one.

231
00:45:23.780 --> 00:45:27.815
Maybe on that day,
late in the afternoon, seconds away,

232
00:45:27.915 --> 00:45:30.713
he'll want to start it all over again...

233
00:45:30.813 --> 00:45:32.880
from the beginning.

234
00:45:32.980 --> 00:45:37.548
He's done it before. Recreated
the whole thing, retold the whole thing.

235
00:45:37.648 --> 00:45:40.731
On a whim. With little differences
that must mean the world to him,

236
00:45:40.831 --> 00:45:43.015
a branch that crooks
in a different direction,

237
00:45:43.115 --> 00:45:46.810
one egg more or less in the nest of a flea.

238
00:45:47.281 --> 00:45:50.127
What a self-centered...

239
00:45:50.227 --> 00:45:52.802
self-indulgent creature he is. Isn't he?

240
00:45:52.902 --> 00:45:56.543
Deaf-mute. Insatiable.

241
00:45:57.480 --> 00:46:00.380
These things he expects of you.

242
00:46:00.480 --> 00:46:02.847
Do you think anyone will care?

243
00:46:02.947 --> 00:46:05.843
Men of 1,000 years from now?

244
00:46:15.663 --> 00:46:18.626
What's it like to be in his presence?

245
00:46:23.747 --> 00:46:26.110
Is there a face?

246
00:46:26.679 --> 00:46:28.510
No.

247
00:46:30.413 --> 00:46:32.244
There is no face.

248
00:46:34.479 --> 00:46:36.943
There is no face.

249
00:46:38.647 --> 00:46:41.543
There's a thing that swallows you.

250
00:46:43.114 --> 00:46:47.510
It holds you together while it's
tearing you apart and it's terrifying.

251
00:46:48.346 --> 00:46:51.214
It makes you feel worthless...

252
00:46:51.313 --> 00:46:54.309
and it makes you want to be worthless.

253
00:46:56.880 --> 00:47:01.343
And all the while, it makes you believe
that you and he are one and the same...

254
00:47:02.514 --> 00:47:05.944
That... that is...

255
00:47:10.380 --> 00:47:12.977
Well, that can be quite confusing.

256
00:47:20.581 --> 00:47:22.715
That's how I remember it, anyway.

257
00:47:22.815 --> 00:47:26.314
It's been a million years since he
so much as looked in my direction.

258
00:47:26.414 --> 00:47:31.177
- Your pride made him angry.
- I'm not proud. I am not proud.

259
00:47:31.913 --> 00:47:34.443
He's the proud one.

260
00:47:38.513 --> 00:47:41.681
- How's our little wager going?
- I do not wager.

261
00:47:41.781 --> 00:47:44.809
Oh, dear me, course not.

262
00:47:52.513 --> 00:47:55.947
- What?
- You already know the outcome, don't you?

263
00:47:56.047 --> 00:48:00.048
- No. Not at all.
- Yes. Yes, you do.

264
00:48:00.148 --> 00:48:02.381
I am able to do that generally, yes.

265
00:48:02.481 --> 00:48:07.043
But when it comes to you
and your little things, not always.

266
00:48:11.747 --> 00:48:15.607
I could tell you what would've happened if
you'd passed by this place a moment earlier.

267
00:48:17.980 --> 00:48:20.342
Would you like to know?

268
00:48:25.179 --> 00:48:27.906
The boy would not have met you.

269
00:48:28.714 --> 00:48:30.780
After the mother's death,

270
00:48:30.880 --> 00:48:34.213
his relationship
with the father deteriorates.

271
00:48:34.313 --> 00:48:39.010
He puts up with it for several years,
expecting that the father will not live long.

272
00:48:39.780 --> 00:48:45.747
Eventually, he poisons the father
and is hanged for it.

273
00:48:45.847 --> 00:48:49.848
Along the way, the boy
has a son who remains here.

274
00:48:49.948 --> 00:48:52.877
Like the grandfather, he loves the desert.

275
00:48:54.980 --> 00:48:57.379
That's how it would have been this time.

276
00:48:58.148 --> 00:49:01.381
In previous tellings of the world,
it was all a little different.

277
00:49:01.481 --> 00:49:05.310
Sometimes it was nothing but love
between the father and the son.

278
00:49:07.280 --> 00:49:10.610
That's how your father amuses himself.

279
00:49:14.513 --> 00:49:17.313
Now it's your turn to take a hand.

280
00:49:17.413 --> 00:49:19.810
Can you do any better?

281
00:49:33.680 --> 00:49:35.913
Why do you live here?

282
00:49:36.013 --> 00:49:39.247
Because the desert is ruthless.

283
00:49:39.347 --> 00:49:43.081
It strips you of your vanities,
your illusions, and...

284
00:49:43.181 --> 00:49:47.048
gives you the opportunity
to see yourself for who you are.

285
00:49:47.647 --> 00:49:50.181
Isn't that why you're here?

286
00:49:50.281 --> 00:49:55.543
Because your god speaks louder here?

287
00:49:56.380 --> 00:49:59.676
God speaks wherever a man wants to listen.

288
00:50:06.213 --> 00:50:08.214
What I said to you about my son...

289
00:50:08.314 --> 00:50:11.280
It doesn't matter that we don't talk.

290
00:50:11.380 --> 00:50:13.414
We're not women.

291
00:50:13.514 --> 00:50:16.576
A father talks through example.

292
00:50:20.347 --> 00:50:23.243
He's the best boy in the world.

293
00:50:25.981 --> 00:50:29.076
Too good, perhaps.

294
00:50:35.713 --> 00:50:39.648
Do you see that? The smooth rock jutting out.

295
00:50:39.748 --> 00:50:41.748
- Just below the crack there.
- The reddish rock?

296
00:50:41.848 --> 00:50:44.881
Yes. That's Jasper stone. I'm sure of it.

297
00:50:44.981 --> 00:50:47.548
I need a sample to take to market.

298
00:50:47.648 --> 00:50:51.714
- I would share any profits with you.
- No, that wouldn't be necessary.

299
00:50:51.814 --> 00:50:56.447
I can't in good conscience allow you
to do more work for nothing.

300
00:50:56.547 --> 00:50:59.977
If you don't want the money,
you give it to the poor.

301
00:51:00.447 --> 00:51:03.042
How would you go about it?

302
00:51:10.113 --> 00:51:12.446
It would take three people.

303
00:51:12.546 --> 00:51:14.747
Two to lower the third.

304
00:51:14.847 --> 00:51:18.569
Yes, that's right.
You and I would lower the boy.

305
00:51:18.669 --> 00:51:20.847
Just to pick at the rock.

306
00:51:20.947 --> 00:51:25.443
And if it's all that I think it is,
I will return with laborers and dig deep.

307
00:51:27.380 --> 00:51:30.476
It could change the course of our lives.

308
00:51:32.813 --> 00:51:35.774
The boy's life, anyway.

309
00:52:02.279 --> 00:52:04.080
I feel better.

310
00:52:04.180 --> 00:52:08.228
You do? Good. That's good.

311
00:52:17.913 --> 00:52:21.242
My mother had this when she was my age.

312
00:52:21.379 --> 00:52:24.209
And then she was fine.

313
00:52:41.880 --> 00:52:45.346
My father, my sisters and I...

314
00:52:45.446 --> 00:52:48.676
once spent a night in Jaffa.

315
00:52:48.778 --> 00:52:51.246
Did I tell you this already?

316
00:52:51.346 --> 00:52:53.709
Tell me again.

317
00:52:54.813 --> 00:52:58.243
My father's cousin put us up by the port.

318
00:52:59.046 --> 00:53:01.480
I could barely sleep...

319
00:53:01.580 --> 00:53:04.609
with the sounds of the city...

320
00:53:04.780 --> 00:53:07.443
dogs barking...

321
00:53:08.046 --> 00:53:10.913
music from a wedding...

322
00:53:11.313 --> 00:53:14.276
men quarreling...

323
00:53:15.179 --> 00:53:17.975
a pig brought to slaughter...

324
00:53:19.213 --> 00:53:22.042
a drunk woman laughing.

325
00:53:22.979 --> 00:53:25.509
And the smells...

326
00:53:28.379 --> 00:53:32.376
pepper, cedar wood...

327
00:53:33.213 --> 00:53:35.176
garum.

328
00:53:51.546 --> 00:53:54.342
If you're ever there...

329
00:53:55.413 --> 00:53:57.410
you think of me.

330
00:53:58.747 --> 00:54:01.076
Yes. I will.

331
00:54:19.346 --> 00:54:23.734
I took her to doctors,
brought doctors to her.

332
00:54:24.181 --> 00:54:29.195
Magicians, quacks. I tried them all.

333
00:54:31.663 --> 00:54:34.226
She's going to die, holy man.

334
00:54:34.846 --> 00:54:38.076
There is nothing to be done about her.

335
00:54:40.363 --> 00:54:43.469
When her eyes close for the last time...

336
00:54:44.863 --> 00:54:48.250
our whole world will come to an end forever.

337
00:54:50.446 --> 00:54:53.971
It's stunning, isn't it?

338
00:54:55.213 --> 00:54:58.009
That life ends.

339
00:55:00.747 --> 00:55:03.309
You will meet again.

340
00:55:10.713 --> 00:55:12.814
We will have been here together.

341
00:55:12.914 --> 00:55:15.710
And we leave the boy behind.

342
00:55:17.146 --> 00:55:19.609
That'll have to do.

343
00:56:38.079 --> 00:56:41.109
How far can a man walk into the desert?

344
00:56:42.479 --> 00:56:44.281
Only halfway.

345
00:56:44.381 --> 00:56:46.975
After that, he's walking out.

346
00:56:56.513 --> 00:56:59.080
When you leave, you could take me with you.

347
00:56:59.180 --> 00:57:01.014
I could pass for your son.

348
00:57:01.314 --> 00:57:03.947
That would be believable, wouldn't it?

349
00:57:04.047 --> 00:57:07.146
Believable, yes, but nevertheless a lie.

350
00:57:07.246 --> 00:57:08.847
But a lie that wouldn't hurt anyone.

351
00:57:08.947 --> 00:57:11.497
My mother and father
wouldn't be there to hear it.

352
00:57:11.597 --> 00:57:14.359
A lie hurts the person who tells it.

353
00:57:20.446 --> 00:57:24.680
You could adopt me.
That way it wouldn't be a lie.

354
00:57:24.780 --> 00:57:28.009
The Romans do it all the time,
adopt each other.

355
00:57:37.480 --> 00:57:40.409
Have you found what you
were looking for out here?

356
00:57:43.712 --> 00:57:46.576
Yes. Yes, I have.

357
00:57:47.580 --> 00:57:50.076
What were you looking for?

358
00:57:53.180 --> 00:57:57.042
I was looking for a place to reflect
and to pray in peace.

359
00:57:58.679 --> 00:58:01.942
A place to look inward and to find myself.

360
00:58:05.413 --> 00:58:08.074
I walk out there, too.

361
00:58:10.446 --> 00:58:12.548
Sometimes when I'm out there,

362
00:58:12.647 --> 00:58:15.543
I feel this thing rising inside of me,

363
00:58:16.480 --> 00:58:19.764
that I am everything
and that everything is me.

364
00:58:20.547 --> 00:58:23.742
That I will always be alive. Forever.

365
00:58:26.879 --> 00:58:31.079
And it's very conceited,
I know, to feel that way.

366
00:58:31.179 --> 00:58:33.775
I'm ashamed of that feeling.

367
00:59:10.413 --> 00:59:13.546
Some wine, holy man?

368
00:59:13.646 --> 00:59:15.709
No. Thank you.

369
00:59:23.446 --> 00:59:26.909
Boy. Boy.

370
01:00:37.412 --> 01:00:40.013
You are an easy target.

371
01:00:40.113 --> 01:00:42.642
Because you're weak.

372
01:01:01.746 --> 01:01:04.921
- How's your mother doing?
- She's feeling better.

373
01:01:05.021 --> 01:01:07.608
She thinks it's passing.

374
01:01:15.179 --> 01:01:17.675
Take your knife, boy.

375
01:01:25.412 --> 01:01:27.976
Just in case.

376
01:02:35.813 --> 01:02:38.547
If I had fallen behind like that,

377
01:02:38.647 --> 01:02:42.408
my father would have caned me
on the soles of my feet.

378
01:03:00.478 --> 01:03:02.308
Come.

379
01:03:19.779 --> 01:03:24.081
I am stronger than 10 men...

380
01:03:24.181 --> 01:03:28.675
and I am taller than 10 men,
but a boy can carry me.

381
01:03:29.012 --> 01:03:31.308
What am I?

382
01:03:33.446 --> 01:03:35.809
It's a riddle.

383
01:03:38.479 --> 01:03:40.647
I am stronger than 10 men,

384
01:03:40.747 --> 01:03:44.222
I'm longer than 10 men,
and a boy can carry me.

385
01:03:44.321 --> 01:03:46.542
What am I?

386
01:03:53.013 --> 01:03:55.242
A rope.

387
01:03:57.112 --> 01:03:59.036
It's a rope.

388
01:04:39.979 --> 01:04:41.876
Come.

389
01:04:42.612 --> 01:04:44.508
Come.

390
01:04:47.029 --> 01:04:49.196
Do you see that piece of rock?

391
01:04:49.296 --> 01:04:51.998
The holy man and I will lower you with rope.

392
01:04:52.098 --> 01:04:56.625
All you have to do is chisel out a piece
and we'll pull you back up.

393
01:04:57.745 --> 01:04:59.642
No.

394
01:05:01.646 --> 01:05:04.445
No. I'm not going down there.

395
01:05:04.545 --> 01:05:06.775
You will.

396
01:05:07.746 --> 01:05:10.680
No. You know I'm afraid
of falling from high places.

397
01:05:10.780 --> 01:05:13.408
That is precisely why you will do it.

398
01:05:14.178 --> 01:05:16.964
I will not do it! I'm not going down there!

399
01:05:17.064 --> 01:05:19.814
You will not disobey me. You will regret it.

400
01:05:19.914 --> 01:05:23.862
He knows I'm scared to death of heights.
What kind of father asks me to do this?

401
01:05:26.313 --> 01:05:28.786
Please. Please, let him go.
Let him go. I can go down.

402
01:05:28.886 --> 01:05:31.608
I'll do it. I'll do it.

403
01:06:14.445 --> 01:06:16.976
I will go down myself.

404
01:06:17.446 --> 01:06:22.208
Do you think it can be done?
Just you and the boy to hold the ropes?

405
01:06:27.111 --> 01:06:28.709
Yes.

406
01:09:20.378 --> 01:09:22.237
Boy!

407
01:09:22.612 --> 01:09:26.387
Cut yourself from the rope.
You too, holy man.

408
01:09:26.747 --> 01:09:30.041
I'll only drag you over if I slip again.

409
01:10:44.845 --> 01:10:46.743
No!

410
01:12:08.478 --> 01:12:10.004
What is it?

411
01:12:13.078 --> 01:12:16.007
What is it? What is it?

412
01:14:33.945 --> 01:14:36.907
I don't want my mother to see him like this.

413
01:16:08.112 --> 01:16:10.974
He looks so much smaller now, doesn't he?

414
01:16:47.878 --> 01:16:49.718
You are a good son.

415
01:18:32.178 --> 01:18:34.279
Your son loves you.

416
01:18:34.378 --> 01:18:36.613
Your son loves you.

417
01:18:36.713 --> 01:18:40.441
Your son loves you.
He is your son and he loves you.

418
01:19:12.012 --> 01:19:15.141
Am I expected to just walk away now?

419
01:19:16.728 --> 01:19:19.557
As if I'd never met these people?

420
01:19:20.377 --> 01:19:23.006
As if they mean nothing to me?

421
01:20:33.645 --> 01:20:35.508
Mother!

422
01:20:37.911 --> 01:20:39.775
Mother!

423
01:24:11.477 --> 01:24:13.374
Go.

424
01:24:14.244 --> 01:24:16.641
Please, go.

425
01:24:29.912 --> 01:24:34.279
If I leave here without a blessing,
I won't make it one night out there.

426
01:24:34.379 --> 01:24:38.177
A boy needs his father's permission
to become a man.

427
01:24:38.277 --> 01:24:40.441
It's perverse, isn't it?

428
01:24:49.977 --> 01:24:52.642
Love God above all things.

429
01:24:55.845 --> 01:24:58.174
Love life.

430
01:25:36.778 --> 01:25:38.245
Show me his destiny.

431
01:25:38.345 --> 01:25:41.207
- Yeshua...
- Show me now!

432
01:26:12.211 --> 01:26:15.812
You could have pulled the father up
and seven heavier men if you'd wanted to.

433
01:26:15.911 --> 01:26:18.140
That's nonsense.

434
01:26:25.311 --> 01:26:27.721
No. She's mine!

435
01:27:21.910 --> 01:27:23.807
No.

436
01:27:47.611 --> 01:27:50.340
Who the hell do you think you are?

437
01:28:41.077 --> 01:28:43.574
This is it for me.

438
01:28:45.295 --> 01:28:48.424
You didn't think I was going
to walk you all the way, did you?

439
01:28:48.944 --> 01:28:51.044
Why here?

440
01:28:51.444 --> 01:28:53.740
My feet hurt.

441
01:29:12.445 --> 01:29:14.546
I'll come to you in the end.

442
01:29:14.646 --> 01:29:17.640
And if you give me a sign
I'll help you down...

443
01:29:17.739 --> 01:29:20.038
and you can stay.

444
01:29:32.261 --> 01:29:34.140
Give my regards to the old man.
